All argument variables of current stack frame or those matching REGEXPs.
Usage: info args [-q] [-t TYPEREGEXP] [NAMEREGEXP]
Prints the argument variables of the current stack frame.
If NAMEREGEXP is provided, only prints the argument variables whose name
matches NAMEREGEXP.
If -t TYPEREGEXP is provided, only prints the argument variables whose type
matches TYPEREGEXP.  Note that the matching is done with the type
printed by the 'whatis' command.
By default, the command might produce headers and/or messages indicating
why no argument variables can be printed.
The flag -q disables the production of these headers and messages.
